lso includes a minimum initial term of 15 years, minimum bill provisions, termination and exit fees, and credit requirements. A CPUC decision is expected in late 2026 or early 2027.","context":"NSP-Wisconsin — NSP-Wisconsin filed a proposed tariff in the second quarter of 2026, which would be mandatory for new loads over 100 MW and requires the customer pay for generation and other infrastructure costs needed to serve the load, if approved as filed. The proposed tariff also includes a minimum initial term of 15 years, minimum bill provisions, termination and exit fees, and credit requirements. A PSCW decision is expected in early 2027.","section":"In addition, the regulatory commissions authorize the ROE, capital structure and depreciation rates in rate proceedings. Decisions by these regulators can significantly impact Xcel Energy’s results of operations.","block":524,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"managementExplanations":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"0fcd1157183d055ae4d8858b59ca6f9bf364f5ebbbea0323ef70813497b8eb05","quote":"In the quarter ended June 30, 2026, NSP-Minnesota recognized reductions in depreciation expense and asset retirement obligations due to nuclear life extensions verbally approved in the Minnesota Electric Rate Case.","context":"(a)Amounts include Sherco Units 1 & 3 and A.S. King for NSP-Minnesota; Comanche Unit 3, Craig Unit 2, Hayden Units 1 and 2 for PSCo; and Tolk Unit 1 and 2 for SPS. Amounts are presented net of accumulated depreciation.","section":"ITEM 1 — FINANCIAL STATEMENTS","block":118,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"5a1ba056b8f4185a55927ebc1b4017d7a32ae2b66a91ab7cd1a2e5a5d6bbce70","quote":"The following discussion and analysis by management focuses on those factors that had a material effect on Xcel Energy’s financial condition, results of operations and cash flows during the periods presented or are expected to have a material impact in the future. It should be read in conjunction with the accompanying unaudited consolidated financial statements and the related notes to consolidated financial statements. Due to the seasonality of Xcel Energy’s operating results, quarterly financial results are not an appropriate base from which to project annual results.","context":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":378,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"eac26b43ac12c34cf7dbf036fc6ba470baa391398e6bcb739f938e33542aaec6","quote":"The demand for electric power and natural gas is affected by seasonal differences in the weather. In general, peak sales of electricity occur in the summer months, and peak sales of natural gas occur in the winter months. As a result, the overall operating results may fluctuate substantially on a seasonal basis. Additionally, Xcel Energy’s operations have historically generated less revenues and income when weather conditions are milder in the winter and cooler in the summer.","context":"The following discussion and analysis by management focuses on those factors that had a material effect on Xcel Energy’s financial condition, results of operations and cash flows during the periods presented or are expected to have a material impact in the future. It should be read in conjunction with the accompanying unaudited consolidated financial statements and the related notes to consolidated financial statements. Due to the seasonality of Xcel Energy’s operating results, quarterly financial results are not an appropriate base from which to project annual results.","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":379,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"14ea5c6f5ef8cd745ad4ae864db1b899b995e92b84752588f29321e404b9ea9a","quote":"The following discussion includes financial information prepared in accordance with GAAP, as well as certain non-GAAP financial measures such as ongoing earnings and ongoing diluted EPS. Generally, a non-GAAP financial measure is a measure of a company’s financial performance, financial position or cash flows that adjusts measures calculated and presented in accordance with GAAP.","context":"Non-GAAP Financial Measures","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":381,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"9aa458cdcb1e7842159146f2b2241d5ee902ab2e2a7eab80e42824b8c629a057","quote":"Xcel Energy’s management uses non-GAAP measures for financial planning and analysis, for reporting results to the Board of Directors, in determining performance-based compensation and communicating its earnings outlook to analysts and investors. Non-GAAP financial measures are intended to supplement investors’ understanding of our performance and should not be considered alternatives for financial measures presented in accordance with GAAP. These measures are discussed in more detail below and may not be comparable to other companies’ similarly titled non-GAAP financial measures.","context":"The following discussion includes financial information prepared in accordance with GAAP, as well as certain non-GAAP financial measures such as ongoing earnings and ongoing diluted EPS. Generally, a non-GAAP financial measure is a measure of a company’s financial performance, financial position or cash flows that adjusts measures calculated and presented in accordance with GAAP.","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":382,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"20177649c84a6bb0c3bb172bcbb395ced5b66907b04a024645cfc7d5327311f4","quote":"Earnings Adjusted for Certain Items (Ongoing Earnings and Ongoing Diluted EPS)","context":"Xcel Energy’s management uses non-GAAP measures for financial planning and analysis, for reporting results to the Board of Directors, in determining performance-based compensation and communicating its earnings outlook to analysts and investors. Non-GAAP financial measures are intended to supplement investors’ understanding of our performance and should not be considered alternatives for financial measures presented in accordance with GAAP. These measures are discussed in more detail below and may not be comparable to other companies’ similarly titled non-GAAP financial measures.","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":383,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"a10650f753f54af8e0744fefc116b5965f23c2d668fb7eb240fd5f0ceaede7ff","quote":"GAAP diluted EPS reflects the potential dilution that could occur if securities or other agreements to issue common stock (i.e., common stock equivalents) were settled. The weighted average number of potentially dilutive shares outstanding used to calculate Xcel Energy Inc.’s diluted EPS is calculated using the treasury stock method.","context":"Earnings Adjusted for Certain Items (Ongoing Earnings and Ongoing Diluted EPS)","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":384,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"89b9da6e08bf532e52930694bb7c8fd18af8d5008714ce280456c0656dbbf22b","quote":"Ongoing earnings reflect adjustments to GAAP earnings (net income) for certain items. Ongoing diluted EPS for Xcel Energy is calculated by dividing net income or loss, adjusted for certain items, by the weighted average fully diluted Xcel Energy Inc. common shares outstanding for the period. Ongoing diluted EPS for each subsidiary is calculated by dividing the net income or loss for such subsidiary, adjusted for certain items, by the weighted average fully diluted Xcel Energy Inc. common shares outstanding for the period.","context":"GAAP diluted EPS reflects the potential dilution that could occur if securities or other agreements to issue common stock (i.e., common stock equivalents) were settled. The weighted average number of potentially dilutive shares outstanding used to calculate Xcel Energy Inc.’s diluted EPS is calculated using the treasury stock method.","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":385,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e"}},{"id":"547b658fde722c407e5f1b2b97005f83bd1a35f51ae8f7e503b27b5ca35d7023","quote":"We use these non-GAAP financial measures to evaluate and provide details of Xcel Energy’s core earnings and underlying performance. For instance, to present ongoing earnings and ongoing diluted EPS, we may adjust the related GAAP amounts for certain items that are non-recurring in nature. We believe these measurements are useful to investors to evaluate the actual and projected financial performance and contribution of our subsidiaries. These non-GAAP financial measures should not be considered as an alternative to measures calculated and reported in accordance with GAAP.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | ITEM 2 — MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":388,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000154","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000154/xel-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6781f80373e96674cdfacf686b9365e.bin","sha256":"702cb120b259f421ef6f87735ac48163d6